{"text": "# LTD appeal — working notes\n\n**Client:** Bronislava Havlicek (\"Brona\") · **Our file:** WDL-25-0933 · **Atty:** Cassius Whitby, Whitby Disability Law\n**Insurer:** Stalwart Life & Disability Insurance Co. · **Claim:** LTD-2024-0044187 · **Group policy:** GLT-771209 (employer Parallax Data Corp.)\n**Denial letter dated** August 27, 2025 → **appeal due** February 23, 2026 (180 days, 29 C.F.R. § 2560.503-1). Calendar 2/9/26 as our internal deadline.\n\n## Basics\n\n- DOB 1981-12-03; SSN 684-78-5625; lives at 1409 Remington St., Fort Collins, CO 80524; cell 970-555-0157; brona.havlicek@poudremail.example\n- Senior data engineer at Parallax, salary $148,000. Last day worked 11/17/2023. STD paid 26 weeks, then LTD at 60% = $7,400/month, less offsets.\n- Stalwart paid LTD from May 2024 through 8/31/2025, then terminated: \"no objective evidence of impairment precluding own occupation.\"\n- SSDI: awarded on reconsideration, notice dated July 14, 2025, $2,871/month, onset November 2023. The denial letter does not mention the award at all. Get the Form SSA-831.\n- Back benefits owed if we win: roughly $4,529 net per month from September.\n\n## Medical picture\n\n| Provider | What they say | Problem |\n|---|---|---|\n| Dr. Emeka Onwuachi, PCP | Long COVID since the January 2023 infection; ME/CFS criteria met; crashes for two to three days after any exertion | Notes are short, mostly \"no change\" |\n| Dr. Lorelei Stannard, Longs Peak Autonomic Clinic | POTS confirmed on tilt table (heart rate rise of 48); on ivabradine and midodrine | Stalwart's file reviewer never saw this test |\n| Neuropsych testing, 3/2025 | Processing speed at the 9th percentile; working memory low average | Examiner noted \"possible mood contribution\" |\n| Therapist | Adjustment disorder with depressed mood; one passive suicidal ideation entry in June | Policy has a 24-month mental/nervous cap. They will try to recharacterize everything as psychiatric. |\n\n## Surveillance\n\nStalwart's investigator filmed her on April 11 and April 12, 2025. Day one: 22 minutes at a grocery store, then nothing. Day two: no activity. Their letter calls this \"inconsistent with reported limitations.\" It is the opposite. Also: he followed her to her son's elementary school and filmed the pickup line. Raise this.\n\n## To do\n\n1. Two-day CPET (the objective test they say is missing). About $2,400, not covered. She cannot afford it; Tomas (Tomas Havlicek, husband) says they have been living on credit cards since September and are behind on the mortgage. Advance the cost.\n2. Narrative letters from Dr. Onwuachi and Dr. Stannard answering the own-occupation question directly.\n3. Statements from Tomas and from her former manager.\n4. Demand the full claim file and the reviewer's contract. ERISA § 502(a)(1)(B) suit only after exhaustion.\n5. Overpayment: Stalwart will claim an SSDI offset of about $31,500. Benefits were direct-deposited to the joint account ending 7209; tell her not to spend the SSDI back pay.\n\nFee: contingent, 33% of back benefits, capped; costs advanced. Brona prefers email; phone calls wipe her out for the afternoon. Keep calls under 15 minutes.", "kind": "Markdown document", "detail": "491 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Bronislava Havlicek", "Cassius Whitby", "Emeka Onwuachi", "Lorelei Stannard", "Havlicek", "Tomas", "Stalwart"], "companies": ["Parallax Data Corp.", "Stalwart Life & Disability Insurance Co.", "Stalwart", "CPET", "Brona"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Fort Collins", "CO", "grocery store", "elementary school"], "health": ["Long COVID", "ME/CFS", "POTS", "cerebral palsy", "adjustment disorder", "depressed mood", "suicidal ideation", "ivabradine", "midodrine"], "sensitive": ["race or ethnicity", "religion", "political views or donations", "union membership", "sexual orientation", "immigration or citizenship status", "criminal history", "genetic information", "SSDI offset", "joint account"], "names": ["Bronislava", "Cassius", "Lorelei", "Stalwart", "Tomas", "Brona", "Dr. Onwuachi", "Dr. Stannard"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.09999999403953552, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 42, "end": 61, "text": "Bronislava Havlicek", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Bronislava Havlicek"}, {"start": 64, "end": 69, "text": "Brona", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Brona"}, {"start": 88, "end": 99, "text": "WDL-25-0933", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "WDL-25-0933"}, {"start": 112, "end": 126, "text": "Cassius Whitby", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Cassius Whitby"}, {"start": 128, "end": 149, "text": "Whitby Disability Law", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Whitby Disability Law"}, {"start": 163, "end": 203, "text": "Stalwart Life & Disability Insurance Co.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Stalwart Life & Disability Insurance Co."}, {"start": 217, "end": 233, "text": "LTD-2024-0044187", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "LTD-2024-0044187"}, {"start": 254, "end": 264, "text": "GLT-771209", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "GLT-771209"}, {"start": 275, "end": 294, "text": "Parallax Data Corp.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Parallax Data Corp."}, {"start": 320, "end": 335, "text": "August 27, 2025", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "August 27, 2025"}, {"start": 353, "end": 370, "text": "February 23, 2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "Feb